    "explanation": "Both parties: the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nThe figures. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02726) charges a cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 and nothing else, and the trip record's platform policy (EV-TRIP-02726) sets the free waiting period in force at 180 seconds and the cancellation fee at SGD 4.50. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02726) reports a single continuous hold inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius of 150 seconds, running 07:20:21 to 07:22:51 — 30 seconds short of the 180 seconds required. That shortfall decides the case.\n\nRider: your dispute succeeds. The first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 07:20:21, 120 seconds after the 'arrived' marker at 07:18:21, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) is not met at the marker; and even on the clock recomputed from that first qualifying fix the dwell is 150 seconds of the required 180. POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the arrival tap or the wait timer that tap starts, so the 271 seconds the platform's own timer ran (07:18:23 to 07:22:54) is not the measured dwell. Under POL-NS-06 the fee is not chargeable on a shortfall, and that clause refunds whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded.\n\nDriver: your points are answered. Your evidence of presence at the pin — 16 consecutive qualifying fixes inside the 50 m radius, the nearest 0.35 m — is accepted; the arrival geofence under POL-NS-02 is satisfied and the dispute then turns on dwell under POL-NS-01(c), which fails. Your argument that POL-NS-09(b) escalates this case because the trip record's wait timer (271 s) and the exported trace (150 s) conflict is rejected: POL-NS-01(c) resolves that conflict by fixing the measurement basis, and POL-NS-12 — which would let the platform's own arrival and wait-timer events stand as an independent carrier — does not apply, because this trip's arrival marker is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO. There is no unresolved contradiction and no escalation. You asked for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.60 if the fee stands; the fee does not stand, because POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it here. The anti-farming check would not have withheld anything in any event (2 no-show terminations in 30 days against 94 completed trips, 2.1%), but no payout arises.\n\nFurther points. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider — the only chat message is the driver's and the rider's own track sits about 740 m from the pin — but neither fact changes the refund, since POL-NS-06 is strict as to rider presence and response. EV-ADVIS-02726-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and is cited only for the absence it is: it carries no deciding fact and does not permit in-geofence intervals to be summed, so the 150-second dwell stands unaccumulated. No false-arrival referral is issued: POL-NS-05 records one only where no qualifying in-geofence fix exists at all (limb (ii)) or where the corrected dwell meets the minimum (limb (iii)); here 16 qualifying fixes exist and the corrected dwell is short, so limb (i) applies and it refunds without a referral. The rider's request for that referral is therefore declined.\n\nConfidence 0.90. The deciding fact — a 150-second dwell against a 180-second minimum — is carried by EV-GPS-02726 and EV-TRIP-02726, both at weight 1.0, and no artifact carrying it is impaired. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00."
